# =========================================================================
# COPYRIGHTED THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL — NEVER COMMIT
#
# Sources/ holds the IEC 60076-7 standard and paywalled IEEE/Elsevier
# papers. Committing them to a public repository is copyright infringement,
# and it is the kind of thing that surfaces during investor or acquirer
# diligence years later. A `git add -A` staged this folder once; the
# pre-commit hook stopped the commit by coincidence rather than by design,
# which is why the CI check below now looks for PDFs explicitly.
# =========================================================================
# Third-party operational data supplied privately by its owner. Not ours to
# publish under any licence, and the single fastest way to destroy a data
# relationship. Working analysis lives in private/, results go in the paper.
*.xlsx
*.xls

Sources/
sources/
literature/
refs/*.pdf

# The manuscript. Unsubmitted work in progress; the LaTeX source and its
# build artefacts do not belong in the software repository. Publish the
# paper through the journal and link to it.
paper/
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.synctex.gz

# Quarantined ML falsification lab. Lives on the orphan branch `ml-lab`, never
# on field-validation or main. CLAUDE.md forbids neural networks in the
# production engine; this keeps that true on the branches that ship.
ml-lab/
